Looking at this problem, I need to determine whether a 3-coloring of $\mathbb{Z}^2$ exists where (1) each color appears infinitely often on infinitely many horizontal lines, and (2) no three collinear points have all three different colors.

**Answer leak check:** The problem statement contains no solutions, hints, or leaked answers. Proceeding to solve.

